WEBVTT

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.460
It's all right.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.290
It'll be all right.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.400
I'm Amakase Minatsu, the head of 
Amakase Detective Agency.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.400
Nice to meet you.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:00.820
The head?

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.150
Nice to meet you.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.210
I might look like a kid, 
but don't worry about that.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.980
Why? Because I'm a robot.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.080
A robot?!

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:16.030
That's right. My brain is that of an 
adult, or actually, a computer!

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.150
So don't worry about the content 
of your request and ask away!

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.650
You're a robot?

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.910
Yes. I'm an HM-A06, Minatsu.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.130
Everyone calls me Amakase Minatsu.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.810
But you look just like a human...

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:38.770
Well, that's because 
I'm so high-tech, that's all.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:42.500
Would you like me to show you
 proof that I'm a robot?!

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.310
Blast off, Rocket Punch!

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.150
You don't have one those, Boss.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.440
Why not?

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.140
Because there'd be all kinds
 of trouble if we gave you one.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.090
For example...

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.710
It'd be as bad as you thinking we had

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.320
plenty of time left on a job 
due at the end of the month

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.930
because it's only the 25th, 
giving us another week,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.860
only to realize that this month 
was actually February.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.690
Come on, if you keep saying 
those strange things,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.780
you'll make our client worry!

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.870
Hello, I'm her assistant, Kohinata Yuzu.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.510
Likewise, Takanashi Yuuhi.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.660
Takanashi is written as
 "Little birds play,"

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.880
and Yuuhi as "the evening sun."

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.080
Nice to meet you!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.050
Um, I'm Yoshino Kiyotaka.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.850
Why don't you have a seat for now?

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:33.820
Yoshino?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.860
<b>A Place We Both Reached</b>

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.290
Here you go.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.170
Thank you.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.740
Um, is it true that she's a robot?

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.650
It's true.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.320
She's an old model though,

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.370
so her specs aren't as innovative, now.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.650
Well, if she's a robot, 
I'd say she's really high-tech...

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:04.260
In her case, it's probably more correct 
to say she's unique than high-tech.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.690
Especially since she has all kinds 
of problems with her specs!

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.170
What are you saying?! 
I don't have prob—

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.270
Are you all right, Boss?!

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.490
My bananamin!

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.790
Yuzu, get me a banana quick!

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.000
Already have one!

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.180
U-Um...

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.140
Please wait a moment.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.610
If our Boss doesn't absorb
 the bananamin in

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:33.450
bananas at regular intervals, 
she stops functioning.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:38.820
Half the reason we work here 
is to take care of her!

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.930
But I've never heard of bananamin.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.330
I know, it's hard to believe, isn't it?

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.200
But it's true.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.360
There are plenty of 
mysterious things in this world

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.600
that don't follow common sense!

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.500
I see...

00:04:58.990 --> 00:04:59.810
Now then.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.580
So, what did you want to 
ask us to investigate?

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.200
I didn't mean to ask 
for an investigation,

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.750
but I was hoping I could 
ask you a few things...

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.590
Suginami-senpai actually 
recommended me to you...

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.020
Oh, Suginami?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.490
In that case, it must be about <i>that</i>.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.210
You're asking about the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.930
that started blooming again, right?

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.070
Huh? How did you know?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.800
It was easy with my brain!

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.470
All right, let's talk.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.840
Yeah. But before that, 
let me make one thing clear.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:33.760
What's that?

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.410
The Everlasting Cherry Blossom
 on Hatsune Island...

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:39.580
is a bona fide magic tree.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.670
So warm!

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.360
It's still winter, right?

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.690
Though it doesn't look like it.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.660
Maybe it really is magic!

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.760
What's gotten into you so suddenly?

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:58.320
I thought you called 
Ricca's story a setting?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.100
Yes, I did, but...

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.760
Looking at all the people 
viewing the flowers here,

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.380
it feels like it wouldn't 
be strange if there

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.100
was magic to make everyone smile.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.570
Excuse me, can I get another tea?

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:13.690
Oh, yes!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.220
Magic to make people smile?

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.130
That sounds just like Aoi-chan.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.060
This is just a what-if, but...

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.860
What would you do if you 
really could use magic?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.890
I'd use magic to make days longer!

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.340
Then I could work all I wanted!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:34.670
You'd work even if you 
could use magic, huh?

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.950
Of course!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.560
There'd be nothing left if you 
took working away from me!

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.580
Would there be nothing left?

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.270
I don't think that's true.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.050
I thought so, too! 
So what would be left?

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.110
Please don't drink your tea after that!

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.380
Waitress, we're ready to order.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.630
Y-Yes!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:03.270
If I could use magic, 
I'd want to do something for Taka-kun.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:06.110
Charles-san, you spoil Nii-san too much.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.010
I don't think that's true.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.420
There's still so much 
I haven't done for him.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:15.050
What are you planning to do?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.920
And you, Himeno-chan?

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.010
What would you do 
if you could use magic?

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:20.300
Me?!

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.690
It's not like I want to do 
anything with Nii-san, or...

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:30.230
If magic did exist, I'm sure

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:34.500
it would be the same as 
strongly wishing for something.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.320
If you don't wish for it and try hard,

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:39.990
then no matter how small it may be,
 it'll never happen.

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:42.190
You may be right.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.280
In other words,

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.690
maybe what we wished for 
that night the cherry blossoms

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.550
bloomed is what we'd like to do with magic?

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.690
What we wished for...

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:57.730
What did you girls wish for?

00:07:57.730 --> 00:07:59.740
I can't say that!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.260
I don't mind saying.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:03.870
Though it would be a little embarrassing.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:06.010
What about you, Katsuragi-san?

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.800
Th-There's no way I could!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:10.990
B-Besides, could you say yours,
 Rukawa-san?!

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:14.170
O-Of course I couldn't say it...

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.480
Amakase Detective Agency

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.650
I see. 
This is the message from the past?

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:29.180
It's true, the date says 
it was sent on April 30th, 1951.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.500
I'm sure there's just 
something wrong with the display.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.900
The text is garbled, too.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:43.380
Um... is what you said about 
the Everlasting Cherry Tree true?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.670
You said it's magic, but I...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:46.600
It's true!

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:50.210
I was a student at 
Kazami Academy back when

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.580
it was last in bloom.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:55.480
I had all kinds of experiences.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.680
With magic?

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:58.550
That's right!

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:02.090
They weren't all good, either. 
Some were bad.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:05.340
I don't know if the Cherry Blossom
 was responsible

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.660
for all of them, though.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.550
It was the same for me.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:14.670
When I was little I met 
a girl with a mysterious power.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.530
Huh? A girl?

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.240
Yeah.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:21.490
She was my best friend. 
She still is, of course.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.910
But she received a strange power

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.510
from wishing on the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.150
What was it she wished for?

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.790
Well, I don't think I can say.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:35.420
She had her share of hardships 
because of that power.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.720
Hardships...

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.250
It just means a lot of things happened

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:42.190
around the Everlasting 
Cherry Blossom in the past.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.700
And they might still be happening now.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:53.330
Um, in the first place, 
what is this magic?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.960
Well... It's something that 
grants shape to people's feelings.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:59.150
That's magic.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.050
You don't believe me, do you?

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.350
I haven't seen it for myself, so...

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.340
You're still not satisfied after receiving

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.810
a message from the past

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:10.890
when the cherry blossoms bloomed?

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.260
If that was done through magic,

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:14.730
then what's the meaning behind it?

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.900
There's one possibility 
I have in mind about that.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:23.800
Do you know about the 
many worlds interpretation?

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.940
You mean parallel worlds?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:28.870
Right.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.810
This world is filled with 
an infinite number of possibilities,

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.210
and they all coexist.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.870
For example, 
there's a world where you visited

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.180
Amakase Detective Agency like this,

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.920
and a world where you didn't.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:46.960
Yes, I understand that, but...

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.760
Which means the following 
interpretation is also possible.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.430
The members of the Newspaper Club
 from another world

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.770
used the Everlasting Cherry Blossom
 to try and communicate

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.740
something to those of you in this world.

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.730
Don't make that face.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:03.420
It's not like I don't have 
any reason backing it.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.740
Was there any reason behind any of that?

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.740
Recently I met someone 
I shouldn't have been able to.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.440
Um... I don't get it...

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.610
You don't need to for now.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.640
You'll have to confront her
 in time yourself.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:21.160
When that time comes, 
gently reach out to her,

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:22.630
Yoshino-kun.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:31.430
Now then, 
that's all I can tell you for now.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.380
We'll do some investigating 
on our end, too,

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:38.510
so if you find any new information,
 let us know, Yoshino-kun.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.550
Yes, I will.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:44.050
Come visit us anytime.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.750
We're never busy anyway.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.380
Bring the Newspaper Club 
members with you, too.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.680
Let's all have tea together.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.790
I'd be happy if you brought 
some bananas with you next time.

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.230
Chocolate bananas work, too.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.000
I prefer pudding!

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:01.030
I'd like Worcestershire senbei!

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.840
The magic of the Cherry Blossom, huh?

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.090
Thank you very much!

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.980
Oh, Kiyotaka-san!

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.550
Oh, Nii-san!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.570
Senpai!

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:26.060
Taka-kun! Come here!

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:55.950
I finally found you.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.250
Um, are you sure you don't 
have the wrong person?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.190
No, I don't. I've been looking 
for you this whole time.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:04.300
Did I do something to you?

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.000
Yes, you did.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.600
I did? What?

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:08.690
This right here.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:09.990
You stole it.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.340
Huh?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.340
You stole my heart.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:21.220
Uh, are you saying... 
You fell in love with me at first sight?

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.560
No, it wasn't love at first sight.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:28.280
We spent a long time with each other 
until our hearts connected.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:32.980
But we only just met today, right?

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:36.630
Yes. It's the first time in this world.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:37.560
H-Huh?

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:40.280
You may not remember it,

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:44.760
but we swore our love 
to each other in our past lives.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.550
Come to club room during lunch.
 Let's eat together.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:05.420
Ricca-san?

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.670
Ricca-san, please wake up.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:19.620
Ricca-san.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:25.910
Oh, Kiyotaka? Morning.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.680
Good morning.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.850
I see. I guess I fell asleep.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.600
Are you getting enough sleep?

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.190
I heard you're busy with work 
for the student council.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.760
Hm, there is that, but lately

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:41.720
I haven't been able to get 
very good sleep, either.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.640
I'm already sleepy in the morning, 
and stay that way...

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.300
I managed to do my best 
until lunch, though...

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:52.900
You seem like you'd just 
boldly sleep through class, though.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:58.380
And still be able to answer 
the question when called on, too.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.050
I wish I could sleep through class, too.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.120
But Charles, our President, and Shiki

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:07.050
all say I can't because 
it'd ruin my image.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.320
It must be rough being 
the school's idol.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:12.760
I don't care what 
other people think, though...

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.160
Aside from you, Kiyotaka.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:20.380
But thanks to that, 
this is the only place I can take a break.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.280
So I'm protecting this place,
 no matter what.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:27.270
And I'm going to be 
my real self while I'm here.

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:28.810
Ricca-san...

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.430
So, let's get on to flirting.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:35.150
I'm not flirting! 
Don't talk like I do it all the time!

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:38.980
Sheesh, you're no fun, Kiyotaka.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.280
That's not the issue here.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:44.290
Besides, today I have 
a bit of news to report.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:48.090
Then I'll forget the flirting, 
but let's have lunch together.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.130
We can talk after that.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:51.160
Here.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.290
Enjoy this lunch filled with love!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.010
Let's eat.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:03.680
Now...

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.510
How is it? Good?

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:11.670
It's great, Ricca-san.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.200
Thank goodness.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:16.890
Here, ah.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.490
No, that's a bit too...

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:19.730
Ah!

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.530
Um...

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.190
Jeez!

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.570
Is it about the Everlasting Cherry Blossom?

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:38.380
Yes. They also told me 
some things about magic.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:39.180
Magic?!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.780
Wh-Why are you so surprised, Ricca-san?

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:42.840
Because!

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:46.530
I never thought I'd hear 
you say "magic," Kiyotaka!

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:51.260
You've finally started to believe me
 about our past lives!

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.020
I'm so happy!

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.230
Th-That's not the case, but...

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.570
But the fact that you're 
talking to me about this

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:02.400
means that you believe me 
more than you used to, right?

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.410
That... may be true, but...

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.630
So I'm happy!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:11.380
I get the feeling the distance 
between us is going to keep shrinking!

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.220
Ricca-san...

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:16.650
Plus, ever since the cherry blossoms bloomed,

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:18.530
I've felt a change of my own.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.690
A change?

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:23.890
I always had mysterious dreams before,

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:26.460
but I could only vaguely recall them.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:29.080
However, ever since it bloomed,

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:33.250
it feels like they've been tuned, 
and now they're even clearer...

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.430
Thanks to that, 
I'm missing sleep, though.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:37.970
What kind of dreams?

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:44.410
A giant escalator descending from the sky.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:48.580
An island in an underground lake 
where cherry blossoms bloom.

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:51.020
A western academy.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:52.950
A city of fog.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.620
A clock tower.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:56.950
And below that...

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:04.450
That's where you were 
a Category 5 mage, right?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.140
Yes. The Lone Cattleya.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.940
A beautiful girl who swore 
her love to you, Kiyotaka.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.840
You're calling yourself beautiful...

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:15.240
Wh-What's wrong with that?! 
I'm not wrong, am I?

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:19.190
No, well... 
I do think you are beautiful, but..

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.050
I'm happy to hear that.

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:28.090
Did your heart just throb for me?

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.340
N-No, I...

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.960
Hey, Ricca-san!

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.860
Sorry.

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:44.030
But I want you to 
know me better, Kiyotaka.

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:48.360
So we need to get on with our investigation
 of the Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree!

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:51.110
You mean right now?

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:52.680
Of course!

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:13.290
You shouldn't move so suddenly 
when you're lacking sleep.

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:17.000
Oh, y-yeah...

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:24.230
U-Um, Ricca-san?

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.300
Can you move now?

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:31.380
Um, this position isn't good...

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:48.250
I never knew another person's 
lips would be so soft.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.600
It was my first time, 
so I was surprised.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:53.100
I'm the one who's surprised!

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.270
R-Right...

00:19:56.730 --> 00:20:01.950
Um, sorry. I just went with the mood.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:03.130
Went with the...

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.250
Yes, I'm really sorry.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:10.690
Um, did it upset you?

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:12.880
No, I'm not upset,

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:14.770
but...

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:18.240
This is something important, isn't it?

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:21.400
I guess that's why I did it...

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:25.420
It felt like there was 
less distance between us,

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:29.540
so my feelings of love 
flowed out more, and...

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:38.260
A-Anyway, from now on, 
don't kiss me out of the blue, okay?

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.420
Okay, I'll be careful from now on.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:47.300
Next time I'll ask, 
"Can I kiss you?" beforehand.

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:33.530
Do you want to play?

00:22:38.720 --> 00:22:39.830
Thank you.

00:22:42.020 --> 00:22:42.820
Sakura?

00:22:43.640 --> 00:22:45.110
What's wrong, Sakura?

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:45.840
Wait.

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:53.450
What's wrong? 
Did something scary happen?

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:08.530
Sakura!

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:13.400
Ricca-san?

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:40.750
<b>The Place of Memories and Beginnings</b>

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.740
What should I...

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:28.920
What should I...

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:31.090
What should I do?

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.420
Shall I tell you a story?

00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:34.290
A story?

00:23:34.630 --> 00:23:37.060
Next time: The Place of 
Memories and Beginnings

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:38.960
I'm going to tell 
a story about the past.

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:39.930
Your setting?
